From 193a99a2bc39c073b764b70460cf75e78af78c0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Catherine Grabar <catherine.grabar@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 23:32:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 05/13] M2 step 1: seeded SimRng for all gameplay randomness
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds systems/sim_rng.gd (class_name SimRng, static API so it works in
--script test mode) and routes every gameplay randi()/randf() call through
it: world gen obstacles, weather roll, crow targeting, chicken AI. Seeded
runs now reproduce exactly — the first brick of the deterministic sim core
(S-5). Adds determinism regression tests (unit suite now 120/120;
integration 20/20). Plan of record: docs/M2_SPEC.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
